<p>Follow these steps to change the one click preset display order.</p>
<p>For optimal ease-of-use, change the order according to setting type 
 and how often you use them.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>You can only change the settings of one click 
 presets with the <img alt="" class="help-icon" height="16" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/NOT_SHARED_ICON.gif" width="16"/> icon depending on the setting for <span class="Term-Soft">Do not allow changing the display order in One Click Preset 
 List</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced Options</span> tab of 
 the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Manage...</span> on 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab. The <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset List</span> dialog box appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the one click preset whose order you want 
 to change, and then click <span class="Term-Soft">Up</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Down</span>.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Only one click 
 presets with the <img alt="" class="help-icon" height="16" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/NOT_SHARED_ICON.gif" width="16"/> icon are displayed in the list depending 
 on the settings for <span class="Term-Soft">Do not allow changing the display 
 order in One Click Preset List</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Advanced 
 Options</span> tabs of the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to save 
 the changes and close the <span class="Term-Soft">Manage One Click Preset 
 List</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
